 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon Relational Database Service API (2014-10-31). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. DB subnet groups, DB parameter groups, DB cluster parameter groups and option groups are stored configuration served over the Query protocol: no DB instance, cluster, proxy, snapshot, event subscription, network or database engine exists, and CreateDBInstance, CreateDBCluster, CreateDBSnapshot and every other official operation return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. Parameter and option values are not modeled: ModifyDBParameterGroup, ResetDBParameterGroup, DescribeDBParameters, the cluster equivalents, CopyDBParameterGroup, ModifyOptionGroup and DescribeOptionGroupOptions are not implemented. Default parameter, option and subnet groups are not pre-created, and parameter group families, major engine versions and subnet IDs are stored without checking that they exist. A subnet group needs 2 to 20 distinct subnet-xxxxxxxx or subnet-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx IDs and is not checked for Availability Zone coverage; it reports no VPC, Availability Zone, Outpost, status or network type. DB subnet group and DB (cluster) parameter group names are stored in lowercase as documented, \"default\" subnet groups are refused, and option groups accept only the documented EngineName values. Describe operations refuse Filters, accept MaxRecords from 20 to 100 and fail with the operation's not-found fault for an unknown name. Tag keys must be present and must not start with aws: or rds:. Tag operations on an unknown ARN fail with DBInstanceNotFound, the first not-found fault the official tag operations model, and ListTagsForResource refuses Filters.",
  "title": "Amazon Relational Database Service (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2014-10-31"
 },
